t{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2}-\\frac{1}{n}{({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the ${x}_{i}$ data:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{x}_{i}=5+7+8+6+9=35.\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{x}_{i}^{2}=255.$\n\nFinally, by substituting into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n{S}_{xx}=255-\\frac{1}{5}(35)^{2}=255-245=10.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512910 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186512731 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512910 #edb/ref 1069 "q-251803" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512910 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512910 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the two sets of $7$ paired observations in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $9$ | $11$ | $12$ | $4$ | $3$ | $2$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $3$ | $9$ | $27$ | $2$ | $4$ | $8$ | $1$ |\n\nGiven that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=494,$ calculate ${S}_{xy}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512910 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8f3d0803-8d23-5ea9-98da-36f1c313a55f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512910 #edb/ref 1074 "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the sum of products of deviations from the means can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}-\\frac{1}{n}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} & =9+11+12+4+3+2+8=49, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} & =3+9+27+2+4+8+1=54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=494.$\n\nFinally, by substituting in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n{S}_{xy}=494-\\frac{1}{7}(49)(54)=494-378=116.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512911 #edb