45485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512955 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider two sets of $20$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{20},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{20}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{x}_{i}=400,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{y}_{i}=440, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{x}_{i}^{2}=8\\,590,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{y}_{i}^{2}=9\\,740.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the sum of the squared deviations from the mean for the points ${x}_{i}.$\n\n${S}_{xx}=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512955 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f69f9435-629a-5550-ae7c-8e46c05363dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512955 #edb/ref 1074 "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the sum of squared deviations from the mean for the data ${x}_{i}$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2}-\\frac{1}{n}{({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given statistics in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & =8\\,590-\\frac{1}{20}(400)^{2} \\\\  & =8\\,590-8\\,000 \\\\  & =590.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
